<title>INDIA: India announces 13.05 pct, 10-yr bonds issue. [CORRECTED 14:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>India announces 13.05 pct, 10-yr bonds issue. [CORRECTED 14:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government on Tuesday announced a 13.05 percent (corrects from 13.5 percent) bonds issue worth 50 billion rupees with a maturity period of 10 years, a government statement said.  </p>
<p>The bonds will be in conversion of treasury bills held by the Reserve Bank of India, it added.</p>
<p>The bonds will be eligible for ready forward facility, the statement said.</p>
</text>
